Subject: monitor mode, say the name of the JACK client

With -M (and -C) a line "client NAME" comes before "ready": the name JACK gave to
the client. Without -u the name carries the process number, and with -u it is
the name asked for unless another client has it already, so a program that
connects the ports must not guess it.
--- a/cmd/rju-play.c
+++ b/cmd/rju-play.c
@@ -723,6 +723,8 @@
 	/* Wait for disk thread to end, which it does when it reaches the
 	   end of the file or is interrupted. */
 	if (d.o.monitor) {
+		/* The name JACK gave: it may differ from the one asked for when another client has it. */
+		printf("client %s\n", jack_get_client_name(d.client));
 		printf("ready %d %g %g %ld\n", d.channels, isr, osr, (long)d.file_frames);
 		fflush(stdout);
 	}
